            <ArticleTitle>Schistosomiasis of the uterus in a patient with dysmenorrhoea and menorrhagia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>106-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Abdominal hysterectomy was performed in a patient because of complaints of dysmenorrhoea and menorrhagia and the uterus was sent for histopathological analysis. Besides adenomyosis an extensive granulomatous infection with Schistosoma mansoni eggs was found.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
